        {
          "id": "blk_86k1g3czg6",
          "type": "text",
          "v": 1,
          "fields": {
            "content": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "· People “Oscar Sharp stands out because there is an original comedic voice at work in his films. His humour is surreal and anarchic, in the best British tradition.” - Sir Alan Parker - Midnight Express, Evita \"One of the best short films I've seen.\" - Ava DuVernay ​ - Selma \"I fucking loved that one.\" - Joss Whedon (re The Stabbington Application) \"The short packs in an amazing amount. You get a little slice of life, a well-developed main character and really touching moments. It is also stunningly edited.” - Mike Newell - Harry Potter, Four Weddings “The direction is amazing...quite beautiful...thanks for pushing the medium forward! In a crazy, beautiful way!” - David Chen - Slash Film “His work has universal appeal because it explores questions that have crossed everybody's minds.” - James King - BBC Radio 1 \"The Kármán Line was exceptional. Most of all Olivia Colman's performance ... I have rarely seen her better.\" - Christopher Priest - Author: The Prestige \"Great stuff.\" - John Hurt - Alien, The Elephant Man “I really like your work.” - Todd Solondz - Happiness, Palindromes \"Incredibly Moving.\" - Paul Haggis - Crash, Million Dollar Baby \"This is a film that people really do need to see.\" - Zoë Ball - BBC Radio 1 “Combines lots of clever techniques to give us a real sense of what the character wants.” - Chris Collins - British Film Institute · Publications​ \"Sharp is a huge talent, masterly with tone and style.\" - The New Yorker - Sarah Larson \"Sharp has established himself as a master of creating extraordinary scenarios, yet at the same time making them feel realistic and human\" - Short Of The Week “The search for Britain’s next great film director is over.” - Sunday Telegraph \"Oscar Sharp’s The Kármán Line is a fascinatingly surreal and moving fantasy-parable.\" - The Guardian - Peter Bradshaw \"Oscar Sharp's The Kármán Line naturally levitates above the pack, a brilliantly executed tragicomedy which simply plays out variations on a single, ingenious idea.\" - Little White Lies \"A quietly devastating film that may be one of the best works of art you’ll see on the big screen this year.\" - Londonist \"Oscar Sharp is a maverick.\" - Flavorpill “Amazing. It was like watching someone’s dream.” - The Observer - Ellie Rowsell of Wolf Alice \"Pairing deadpan tonality with the outlandish imagination of a Roald Dahl story, it’s not often that a movie so bizarre in conception succeeds so well in execution, and Sharp might very well be set to follow his protagonist’s skyward trajectory.\" - Filmcomment.com \"Suggests the future of the British film Industry may be in safe hands\" - The List \"This movie says in 5 mins what most hollywood movies can't say in 90 mins.\" - Most 'liked' YouTube comment ·"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
